  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: scope-guard.sh resolves the worktree from the written file, so a subagent writing in a child worktree is held to the task scope",
  "spec": "Goal T-1403, wave 2, plan label D2 (prepares D1, subagents in execute workers).\n\nU5, resolved enough for this hook (2026-10-01):\n- Hooks reach subagents: project PreToolUse hooks fire for tool calls made by Agent-tool subagents. Observed in\n  this repo on 2026-10-01: .claude/hooks/planner-mode.sh blocked Bash calls made by a Planner subagent.\n- Environment reaches subagent hooks: subagents run inside the same claude process; that subagent saw the parent's\n  CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. Workers get ORCH_TASK_ID and ORCH_ROOT from spawn.py:1306-1307, so a worker's subagents\n  and their hooks see the same values.\n- NOT verified: the hook process cwd for a worktree-isolated subagent, and where Claude Code places the child\n  worktree (believed .claude/worktrees/<name> inside the repo). The hook must therefore not depend on its own cwd\n  or on the child's location; rely only on tool_input.file_path, ORCH_TASK_ID/ORCH_ROOT, and git.\n\nFacts (main 355583c):\n- .claude/hooks/scope-guard.sh: task id from _lib.sh task_id() (ORCH_TASK_ID, else basename of the cwd toplevel\n  when it matches T-NNNN); wt=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel) of the HOOK's cwd; rel=${file#\"$wt\"/}; bash\n  pattern match against .scope[] of .orchestrator/tasks/<id>.json. A file in a child worktree is therefore\n  measured against whichever worktree the hook happens to run in: in-scope writes are wrongly blocked when the cwd\n  is the parent, and when ORCH_TASK_ID is absent and the cwd is a child whose basename is not T-NNNN, task_id is\n  empty and every write is allowed.\n- .claude/settings.json runs scope-guard.sh for matcher \"Edit|Write\" (settings.json is a protected path; do not\n  edit it).\n- tests/test_hooks.py::test_scope_guard (~15-23) pins: in-scope ok, out-of-scope exit 2 with 'outside task' on\n  stderr, no task id -> exit 0. Keep those assertions passing.\n\nChange (scope-guard.sh):\n1. Resolve the file to a physical absolute path (relative paths against the payload's .cwd when present, else\n   $PWD), as today.\n2. Find the work tree that contains the file: git -C <nearest existing ancestor directory of the file>\n   rev-parse --show-toplevel. If none, or if that tree's `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` (resolved) differs from\n   the task worktree's (the task's .worktree from the task JSON, else the hook cwd's toplevel), the file is outside\n   the task: exit 2 with the same 'outside task' message.\n3. rel = path relative to the containing work tree (child or task worktree), then the existing scope match.\n4. Task id: ORCH_TASK_ID first; else a /wt/T-NNNN/ path component of the file or of the payload .cwd; else the\n   existing basename rule; still exit 0 when none is found (Planner session; planner-mode.sh owns that case).\nKeep it bash + jq + git + python3 like the current script; no new dependencies. A hook must stay fast (one or two\ngit calls).\n\nTests: add test_scope_guard_child_worktree next to test_scope_guard: build the task worktree with git init + one\ncommit, `git worktree add` a child, write the task JSON scope via bus.create_task like test_scope_guard does, call\nhook('scope-guard.sh', ...) with cwd set to each tree. Update test_scope_guard only if the message text changes.\n\nOut of scope: guardrails.sh, settings.json, NotebookEdit coverage, E7 grant_scope.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused tests in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate. Write tests as unittest.TestCase methods using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1436"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_hooks.py::test_scope_guard_child_worktree: passes: with ORCH_TASK_ID set and a child git worktree added from the task worktree, scope-guard.sh exits 0 for an in-scope file inside the child worktree and 2 for an out-of-scope file there, whether the hook runs with cwd = task worktree or cwd = child worktree, and exits 2 for a file inside an unrelated git repository",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    ".claude/hooks/scope-guard.sh",
    "tests/test_hooks.py"
  ],
