  "result": {
    "summary": "The hook meets the acceptance criteria. It fails closed when git probing fails, and it resolves symlinks and `..` with realpath. The same-repo check follows the spec's common-dir rule, but that rule leaves a gap (first comment). I did not run the tests. I read the committed script and test file in wt/T-1436, and `git diff` against the base printed nothing.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": ".claude/hooks/scope-guard.sh",
        "line": 58,
        "issue": "The ownership check compares only `git-common-dir`. Every worktree of the repo shares it: the main checkout, other tasks' `wt/T-*` trees, and sibling child worktrees. A file in another task's worktree or in the main checkout is therefore matched by its own relative path against this task's scope. A write to `wt/T-9999/src/x.ts` is allowed if this task's scope has `src/**`. The spec asks for exactly this check, but the gap is worth recording. A tighter rule would also require the containing tree to be the task worktree or a child created under it.",
        "severity": "med"
      },
      {
        "path": ".claude/hooks/scope-guard.sh",
        "line": 22,
        "issue": "With no `ORCH_TASK_ID`, the task id comes from a `/wt/T-NNNN/` component of the file path, and that component can be any task. A worker can pick whose scope applies by choosing its target path. This is only a fallback and the spec asks for it. In normal operation workers have `ORCH_TASK_ID` set.",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "path": "tests/test_hooks.py",
        "line": 51,
        "issue": "The unrelated-repo assertion is weak. `unrelated/src/foreign.ts` would also exit 2 if the common-dir check were removed, because the absolute `rel` would not match `src/**`. Use a scope glob that would match the absolute path (e.g. `**`), or a repo path whose relative form is in scope such as `unrelated/src/...` against a `src/**` scope with the repo root equal to `src`. Either makes the test fail if the common-dir check regresses. There is also no case with `ORCH_TASK_ID` unset and the path-derived task id.",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "path": ".claude/hooks/scope-guard.sh",
        "line": 9,
        "issue": "The hook starts about six python3 processes plus three git calls per Edit/Write. The spec asks for one or two git calls and a fast hook. The extra python3 startups add latency but are not a correctness problem.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
